config HILOG
    tristate "Hilog support"
    default y
    help
      hilog buffer manager.

      Hilog is a simple log manager for OpenHarmonyOS.
      log string write to /dev/hilog, and the hilog driver copy it
      to the ring buffer. Ring buffer can be read from userspace.

config HILOG_BUFFER_SIZE
    int "hilog buffer size"
    default 262144
    help
      Define the default ring buffer size of hilog. 256 KiB chosen to retain
      enough boot/panic context for kernel debugging on QEMU dev trees while
      remaining tractable on memory-constrained targets (Hi3516 has ~32 MiB
      RAM, this default uses < 1%). Embedded products may override downward
      via their product kconfig if memory pressure demands.